/-!
# The ATLAS 111-dimensional matrices for the Lyons group

These are the matrices `LyG1-f5r111B0.m1` and `LyG1-f5r111B0.m2` from
R. A. Wilson et al., ATLAS of Finite Group Representations:
https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/matrep/LyG1-f5r111B0

Each row is stored as a natural number with the column entries as its base-five
digits, least significant digit first. The MeatAxe source files and a lossless
transcription script are in `Atlas111Source/`. Inverse candidates are stored
by columns: `atlasAInvMatrix` is the first source matrix, and `atlasBInvMatrix`
is the fourth power of the second source matrix, computed modulo five by that
script. Their inverse identities are proved separately, without trusting the
script. Column storage permits efficient verified dot-product calculations.

The matrices retain the source's row and column order. We use ordinary matrix
multiplication; no permutation-action convention or transposition is involved.
The underlying representation was constructed in W. Meyer, W. Neutsch and
R. Parker, "The minimal 5-representation of Lyons' sporadic group", Math. Ann.
272 (1985), 29–39, DOI: 10.1007/BF01455926. The ATLAS does not record the
contributor of this particular pair of standard generators.
-/

namespace Lyons

